# Managed by host/ansible/roles/chrony. The time contract is coordinator#11.
#
# A drop-in rather than a replacement chrony.conf, so the vendor's upstream sources
# stay as they are and work whenever the bench network is up.

# The seconds source: the DS3234's own time, served by coord-rtc-feed over a SOCK
# datagram. THE CHIP, NOT UTC, and that is what makes this work. coord-rtc takes the
# sample at the chip's seconds rollover, which is the same instant as the falling edge
# of the 1 Hz below -- so this reference and the pulse it is locked to are the same
# clock and agree by construction.
#
# Reporting UTC here instead would make the reference a different clock from the pulse,
# and their difference -- the chip's arbitrary phase against the UTC second -- would
# drift at 2 ppm until it crossed chrony's 0.4 s locked-PPS tolerance and every pulse
# was silently discarded. UTC is a label on this time base, not the base itself;
# coordinator-mavlink logs the FC's GPS-derived offset per session for that.
#
# precision 2e-3 is this path's error: the second boundary is found by polling the
# seconds register, so the poll interval bounds it.
refclock SOCK {{ coord_rtc_chrony_sock }} refid DS32 precision 2e-3 poll 4

# The buffered 1 Hz on GPIO24, and the reason the circuit exists. lock=DS32 pairs each
# edge with a chip sample: the chip says which second, the edge says where the second
# starts. Without a lock chrony discards every pulse until it is already synchronised
# to something.
#
# This is what conditions the clock the cameras align against. libcamera's rpi.SyncMode
# converges the pods' shutters by advertising when the next frame is due, so its
# accuracy is bounded by how well their clocks agree -- and every pod takes a buffered
# copy of THIS edge, so the part of the edge's absolute position that is wrong is
# common-mode and cancels between them. NTP over the gadget link cannot do that: its
# error is per-pod and adds.
refclock PPS /dev/pps0 refid PPS lock=DS32 precision 1e-7 poll 2

# Serve the campods over the USB gadget network. They have no connection to the
# DS3234 and no FC link, so this plus their own buffered PPS leg is their whole time
# source.
#
# Derived from the coordinator's address rather than a second subnet variable, which
# vars/gadget-net.yml says not to add. The role asserts the prefix is 24 so this
# derivation cannot quietly become wrong.
allow {{ campod_gadget_coordinator_ip.rsplit('.', 1)[0] }}.0/{{ campod_gadget_prefix }}
